---
import InternalLayout from '../../layouts/InternalLayout.astro';
---
<InternalLayout title="Permits">
  <div class="an-hero">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Prospecting</p>
      <h1>Permits</h1>
      <p class="lede">Supplier reports and public permit research, together in one place.</p>
      <p><a href="#an-permit-h">Permit leads</a> · <a href="#an-supplier-h">Supplier permit list</a></p>
    </div>
    <div class="an-hero-actions"><button class="btn btn-ghost" type="button" data-refresh>Refresh</button></div>
  </div>
  <section class="an-section" aria-labelledby="an-permit-h">
    <div class="an-head">
      <div><p class="kicker">Public records</p><h2 id="an-permit-h">Permit leads</h2></div>
      <span class="an-meta" data-permit-window>—</span>
    </div>
    <p class="an-note">Building permits from Clark County and the City of Vancouver, joined to county parcel records and state contractor licenses. This is research, not customers: nothing here is a lead or a quote until you act on it. Contractor matches are by exact name, so check one before you call. Same-size window replacements usually need no permit, so these lists miss most simple replacement jobs.</p>
    <p class="an-callout" data-permit-message hidden></p>
    <div class="an-stats" data-permit-stats hidden>
      <article class="an-stat"><span>New-home permits</span><strong data-permit="newHomes">—</strong><small data-permit="newHomesNote">—</small></article>
      <article class="an-stat"><span>Builders</span><strong data-permit="builders">—</strong><small data-permit="buildersNote">—</small></article>
      <article class="an-stat"><span>Remodel and addition permits</span><strong data-permit="remodels">—</strong><small data-permit="remodelsNote">—</small></article>
      <article class="an-stat"><span>Homes built 2011–2016</span><strong data-permit="young">—</strong><small>among those remodel permits</small></article>
    </div>
    <div class="an-grid" data-permit-grid hidden>
      <article class="an-panel"><h3>New-home permits per month</h3><div class="an-chart" data-chart="permitMonthly"></div></article>
      <article class="an-panel"><h3>Biggest builders by permits</h3><div class="an-chart" data-chart="permitBuilders"></div></article>
      <article class="an-panel an-wide">
        <h3>Builders and lot owners</h3>
        <p class="an-note">The lot owner is usually the builder or its project company; the permit applicant is often a permit service or engineer. "30 days" and "90 days" count permits issued in that time.</p>
        <div class="an-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Builders and lot owners table (scroll sideways)">
          <table class="an-table an-table-wide">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Builder</th><th scope="col">Permits</th><th scope="col">30 days</th><th scope="col">90 days</th><th scope="col">Subdivisions</th><th scope="col">State license</th><th scope="col">Phone</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody data-builder-rows></tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="an-panel"><h3>Remodel permits: what fits</h3><div class="an-chart" data-chart="permitSignals"></div></article>
      <article class="an-panel"><h3>Remodel permits: decade the home was built</h3><div class="an-chart" data-chart="permitDecades"></div></article>
      <article class="an-panel an-wide">
        <h3>Remodel and addition list</h3>
        <p class="an-note">Owner names and mailing addresses come from the county assessor. Use them for mail, not unsolicited calls or texts: Washington restricts those. Best fit first; "fit" counts how many of five signals apply (single-family, owner applied, addition, permit in last 90 days, sold in last 2 years).</p>
        <button class="btn btn-ghost" type="button" data-homeowners-load>Show the list</button>
        <div class="an-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Remodel and addition list table (scroll sideways)" data-homeowners-wrap hidden>
          <table class="an-table an-table-wide">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Address</th><th scope="col">Permit</th><th scope="col">Work</th><th scope="col">Built</th><th scope="col">Owner</th><th scope="col">Owner mail</th><th scope="col">Sold</th><th scope="col">Fit</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody data-homeowner-rows></tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="an-section" aria-labelledby="an-supplier-h">
    <div class="an-head">
      <div><p class="kicker">Supplier list</p><h2 id="an-supplier-h">Supplier permit list</h2></div>
      <span class="an-meta" data-supplier-window>—</span>
    </div>
    <p class="an-note">The weekly permit report from Mark's supplier (Construction Monitor), joined to county parcels, sales and state contractor licenses, and compared with the permit leads and mail pilot lists. The report is licensed to the supplier for their own use: keep it inside Clearview and do not forward or post it. This is research, not customers.</p>
    <p class="an-callout" data-supplier-message hidden></p>
    <div class="an-stats" data-supplier-stats hidden>
      <article class="an-stat"><span>Permits this load</span><strong data-supplier="permits">—</strong><small data-supplier="permitsNote">—</small></article>
      <article class="an-stat"><span>New to our lists</span><strong data-supplier="fresh">—</strong><small data-supplier="freshNote">—</small></article>
      <article class="an-stat"><span>With an owner phone</span><strong data-supplier="phones">—</strong><small>printed in the report</small></article>
      <article class="an-stat"><span>County parcel found</span><strong data-supplier="parcels">—</strong><small data-supplier="parcelsNote">—</small></article>
    </div>
    <div class="an-grid" data-supplier-grid hidden>
      <article class="an-panel"><h3>Permits by type</h3><div class="an-chart" data-chart="supplierGroups"></div></article>
      <article class="an-panel"><h3>Remodel, ADU and re-roof: what fits</h3><div class="an-chart" data-chart="supplierSignals"></div></article>
      <article class="an-panel an-wide">
        <h3>New-home builders in the report</h3>
        <p class="an-note">"Projects" opens the builder's own permits from this report, with the permit number, address and subdivision. "Metro rank" is the builder's place in the report's year-to-date ranking of single-family builders for the whole metro area; the report prints shortened names, so a match is by the start of the name. "Already tracked" means the same company is in the Permit leads builders on this page; the report cuts long names off and those match by the start of the name, so read the tracked name shown. A license is shown only when the name matches a state record exactly (ignoring punctuation and LLC or INC).</p>
        <div class="an-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="New-home builders in the report table (scroll sideways)">
          <table class="an-table an-table-wide an-table-list">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Builder</th><th scope="col">Permits</th><th scope="col">Value</th><th scope="col">Last permit</th><th scope="col">Metro rank</th><th scope="col">Already tracked</th><th scope="col">State license</th><th scope="col">Phone</th><th scope="col">Projects</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody data-supplier-builder-rows></tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="an-panel an-wide">
        <h3>Permit list</h3>
        <p class="an-note">Owner names, mailing addresses and phone numbers come from the report and the county assessor. Use mail for homeowners: Washington restricts unsolicited calls and texts, so phone an owner only if they asked to hear from us. Best fit first; "fit" counts how many of five signals apply (single-family, no contractor named, addition or ADU, permit in the last 90 days, sold in the last 2 years) and applies to remodel, ADU and re-roof permits only. It is a sort order, not a prediction. "Connected to" lists the same project in our other records, each with its number and name: the Permit leads case (same permit, or same address with a different permit), the Mail pilot property, a Clearview quote or job at the same street (opens its page), and the builder when we already track it.</p>
        <div class="an-actions">
          <label class="an-field"><span>Show</span><select data-supplier-group></select></label>
          <button class="btn btn-ghost" type="button" data-supplier-load>Show the list</button>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/internal/api/supplier-permits?view=csv" data-supplier-csv download>Download as spreadsheet</a>
        </div>
        <div class="an-table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Permit list table (scroll sideways)" data-supplier-wrap hidden>
          <table class="an-table an-table-xwide an-table-list">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Address</th><th scope="col">Permit</th><th scope="col">Work</th><th scope="col">Connected to</th><th scope="col">Owner</th><th scope="col">Owner mail</th><th scope="col">Owner phone</th><th scope="col">Contractor</th><th scope="col">Home</th><th scope="col">Sold</th><th scope="col">Fit</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody data-supplier-rows></tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="an-note" data-supplier-count hidden></p>
        <p class="an-note">Every phone number has a <strong>Log call</strong> button. Write down what happened; if someone asks not to be contacted, choose that and the number goes on the do-not-contact list for every permit. A number on that list is never a link and the spreadsheet marks it.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <dialog class="an-dialog" data-contact-dialog aria-labelledby="an-contact-h">
    <div class="an-dialog-head"><div><p class="kicker" data-contact-who>Phone number</p><h3 id="an-contact-h" data-contact-number>—</h3></div><button class="btn btn-ghost" type="button" data-contact-close>Close</button></div>
    <p class="an-callout" data-contact-state role="status" hidden></p>
    <form data-contact-form>
      <label class="an-field"><span>What happened</span><select name="outcome" data-contact-outcome required></select></label>
      <label class="an-field"><span>Note (optional)</span><input name="note" maxlength="500" autocomplete="off" /></label>
      <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit" data-contact-save>Save call</button>
    </form>
    <div class="an-dialog-block">
      <form data-contact-block-form>
        <label class="an-field"><span data-contact-block-label>Why</span><input name="why" maxlength="500" autocomplete="off" data-contact-block-input /></label>
        <button class="btn btn-ghost" type="submit" data-contact-block-save>Add to the do-not-contact list</button>
      </form>
    </div>
    <h4>History for this number</h4>
    <ul class="an-history" data-contact-history></ul>
  </dialog>

  <p class="an-status" data-status role="status">Loading permits…</p>
</InternalLayout>
<script>
  import { barChart, columnChart } from '../../lib/charts';
  import { fetchJson, isSessionExpired } from '../../lib/internal-fetch';
  import { loadFailedNode, loadFailureMessage } from '../../lib/load-failed';
  import { formatCents } from '../../lib/money';
  type Row = { label: string; value: number };
  type PermitBuilder = {
    name: string; applicants: string[]; permits: number; lots: number; subdivisions: string[]; jurisdictions: string[];
    lastIssued: string; issued30d: number; issued90d: number;
    license: { match: string; business: string; number: string; phone: string; address: string; principal: string; status: string; expires: string } | null;
  };
  type PermitSummary = {
    status: 'ok' | 'empty' | 'unavailable';
    meta?: Record<string, string>;
    homeowners?: { total: number; signals: { key: string; label: string; value: number }[]; decades: Row[]; absentee: number; built2011to2016: number };
    newHomes?: { permits: number; entities: number; repeatEntities: number; licenseMatched: number; byMonth: Row[] };
    builders?: PermitBuilder[];
  };
  type HomeownerLead = {
    id: string; permitDate: string; status: string; workType: string; address: string; yearBuilt: number | null; sqft: number | null;
    owner: string; ownerMailing: string; absentee: boolean; ownerApplied: boolean; lastSaleDate: string; lastSaleCents: number | null; signals: string[]; score: number;
  };
  type SupplierConnection = { kind: string; label: string; number: string; name: string; detail: string; how: string; href: string };
  type SupplierBuilder = {
    key: string; name: string; permits: number; valueCents: number; lastDate: string; tracked: string; related: string;
    metro: { rank: number; homes: number; rows: number } | null;
    license: { number: string; business: string; status: string; expires: string; match: string } | null;
    phone: string;
  };
  type SupplierSummary = {
    status: 'ok' | 'empty' | 'unavailable';
    meta?: { imported_at: string; edition: string; edition_start: string; edition_end: string; xref_asof: string };
    totals?: { permits: number; pending: number; withOwnerPhone: number; known: number; inPermitLeads: number; inMailPilot: number; newToLists: number; parcelMatched: number; inClearviewWork: number };
    groups?: { key: string; label: string; value: number }[];
    scored?: { total: number; signals: { key: string; label: string; value: number }[] };
    editions?: { edition: string; permits: number }[];
    builders?: SupplierBuilder[];
  };
  type SupplierRow = {
    id: string; pending: boolean; group: string; groupLabel: string; city: string; permitType: string; valueCents: number | null; address: string; permitDate: string;
    owner: string; ownerPhone: string; ownerMailing: string; builder: string; builderPhone: string; builderLicense: string;
    yearBuilt: number | null; sqft: number | null; absentee: boolean; ownerDiffers: boolean; lastSaleDate: string; lastSaleCents: number | null;
    stateLicense: { number: string; status: string } | null; trackedBuilder: string; relatedBuilder: string; inPermitLeads: string; mailPilot: string; score: number;
    subdivision: string; connections: SupplierConnection[];
  };
  const nf = new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US');
  const dollars = (cents: number | null | undefined) => (typeof cents === 'number' ? formatCents(cents) : '—');
  const count = (value: number | null | undefined) => (typeof value === 'number' ? nf.format(value) : '—');
  const $ = (selector: string) => document.querySelector(selector);

  /**
   * Charts are drawn at the width their box actually has, so text stays readable
   * on a phone, and redrawn when that width changes. Each chart registers a
   * builder here; `paint()` runs them all.
   */
  type ChartJob = { build: (width: number) => string; empty: string };
  const jobs = new Map<string, ChartJob>();
  const widths = new Map<string, number>();

  // SVG from our own builders is parsed and imported as nodes; nothing is assigned as HTML.
  function mountSvg(host: HTMLElement, markup: string): boolean {
    const doc = new DOMParser().parseFromString(markup, 'image/svg+xml');
    const root = doc.documentElement;
    if (!root || root.nodeName !== 'svg' || doc.querySelector('parsererror')) return false;
    host.replaceChildren(document.importNode(root, true));
    return true;
  }

  function paintOne(name: string, job: ChartJob) {
    const host = $(`[data-chart="${name}"]`);
    if (!(host instanceof HTMLElement)) return;
    const width = Math.floor(host.clientWidth || host.parentElement?.clientWidth || 320);
    widths.set(name, width);
    const markup = job.build(width);
    if (markup && mountSvg(host, markup)) return;
    const p = document.createElement('p');
    p.className = 'an-empty';
    p.textContent = job.empty;
    host.replaceChildren(p);
  }

  function setChart(name: string, job: ChartJob) {
    jobs.set(name, job);
    paintOne(name, job);
  }

  function clearChart(name: string, message: string) {
    setChart(name, { build: () => '', empty: message });
  }

  let repaintQueued = false;
  function repaintOnResize() {
    if (repaintQueued) return;
    repaintQueued = true;
    requestAnimationFrame(() => {
      repaintQueued = false;
      for (const [name, job] of jobs) {
        const host = $(`[data-chart="${name}"]`);
        if (host instanceof HTMLElement && Math.abs(host.clientWidth - (widths.get(name) ?? 0)) > 8) paintOne(name, job);
      }
    });
  }
  window.addEventListener('resize', repaintOnResize, { passive: true });

  function setText(selector: string, text: string) {
    const el = $(selector);
    if (el instanceof HTMLElement) el.textContent = text;
  }

  function show(selector: string, visible: boolean) {
    const el = $(selector);
    if (el instanceof HTMLElement) el.hidden = !visible;
  }

  const shortDate = (iso: string) => (/^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$/.test(iso) ? new Date(`${iso}T12:00:00`).toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'short', day: 'numeric', year: '2-digit' }) : '—');
  const monthLabel = (ym: string) => (/^\d{4}-\d{2}$/.test(ym) ? new Date(`${ym}-01T12:00:00`).toLocaleDateString('en-US', { month: 'short' }) : ym);

  function appendRow(body: HTMLElement, cells: (string | HTMLElement)[]) {
    const tr = document.createElement('tr');
    cells.forEach((value, i) => {
      const cell = document.createElement(i === 0 ? 'th' : 'td');
      if (i === 0) cell.setAttribute('scope', 'row');
      if (typeof value === 'string') cell.textContent = value;
      else cell.append(value);
      tr.append(cell);
    });
    body.append(tr);
  }

  // ---------- do not contact + call log ----------
  // Numbers on the do-not-contact list are never drawn as a link. The set is loaded before the lists are drawn and again after every save.
  const blockedPhones = new Set<string>();
  const OUTCOMES: [string, string][] = [['reached', 'Spoke with them'], ['no_answer', 'No answer'], ['voicemail', 'Left a voicemail'], ['wrong_number', 'Wrong number'], ['interested', 'Interested, wants to hear more'], ['asked_not_to_call', 'Asked not to be contacted']];
  const phoneDigits = (raw: string) => {
    let digits = raw.replace(/\D/g, '');
    if (digits.length === 11 && digits.startsWith('1')) digits = digits.slice(1);
    return digits.length === 10 && /^[2-9]/.test(digits) ? digits : '';
  };
  const prettyPhone = (digits: string) => `(${digits.slice(0, 3)}) ${digits.slice(3, 6)}-${digits.slice(6)}`;
  type ContactLog = { id: number; phone: string; permitId: string; who: string; outcome: string; outcomeLabel: string; note: string; at: string };

  async function loadContacts() {
    try {
      const result = await fetchJson<{ blocked?: { phone: string }[] }>('/internal/api/supplier-permits?view=contacts', { headers: { accept: 'application/json' } });
      blockedPhones.clear();
      for (const b of result.blocked ?? []) blockedPhones.add(b.phone);
    } catch {
      // Without the list nothing can be marked; the log button still opens, and the server refuses a blocked number.
    }
  }

  // Phone numbers come from the report or a public license record as 10 digits; anything else is shown as plain text, never linked.
  // A do-not-contact number is plain text with a label. Every valid number gets a button for the call log.
  function phoneCell(raw: string, options: { who?: 'owner' | 'builder'; permitId?: string; link?: boolean } = {}): string | HTMLElement {
    const digits = phoneDigits(raw);
    if (!digits) return raw || '—';
    const wrap = document.createElement('span');
    wrap.className = 'an-phone';
    const blocked = blockedPhones.has(digits);
    if (blocked || options.link === false) {
      wrap.append(prettyPhone(digits));
    } else {
      const link = document.createElement('a');
      link.href = `tel:+1${digits}`;
      link.textContent = prettyPhone(digits);
      wrap.append(link);
    }
    if (blocked) {
      const tag = document.createElement('strong');
      tag.className = 'an-dnc';
      tag.textContent = 'Do not contact';
      wrap.append(' ', tag);
    }
    const button = document.createElement('button');
    button.type = 'button';
    button.className = 'btn btn-ghost an-phone-btn';
    button.textContent = blocked ? 'History' : 'Log call';
    button.setAttribute('aria-label', `${blocked ? 'Open the history of' : 'Log a call to'} ${prettyPhone(digits)}`);
    button.addEventListener('click', () => void openContact(digits, options.who ?? 'other', options.permitId ?? ''));
    wrap.append(button);
    return wrap;
  }

  const contactDialog = () => $('[data-contact-dialog]');
  let contactNumber = '';
  let contactWho = 'other';
  let contactPermit = '';

  const contactNote = (text: string) => { setText('[data-contact-state]', text); show('[data-contact-state]', text !== ''); };

  async function post(payload: Record<string, unknown>): Promise<{ ok: boolean; error?: string }> {
    try {
      await fetchJson('/internal/api/supplier-permits', { method: 'POST', headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json', accept: 'application/json' }, body: JSON.stringify(payload) });
      return { ok: true };
    } catch (error) {
      return { ok: false, error: loadFailureMessage(error, 'Could not save. Try again.') };
    }
  }

  async function paintContact() {
    const history = $('[data-contact-history]');
    const blocked = blockedPhones.has(contactNumber);
    setText('[data-contact-number]', prettyPhone(contactNumber));
    setText('[data-contact-who]', contactWho === 'owner' ? 'Owner phone' : contactWho === 'builder' ? 'Contractor phone' : 'Phone number');
    show('[data-contact-form]', !blocked);
    contactNote(blocked ? 'This number is on the do-not-contact list. Do not call or text it.' : '');
    const label = $('[data-contact-block-label]');
    const save = $('[data-contact-block-save]');
    const input = $('[data-contact-block-input]');
    if (label) label.textContent = blocked ? 'Why take it off the list? (required)' : 'Why add it? (optional)';
    if (save) save.textContent = blocked ? 'Take off the do-not-contact list' : 'Add to the do-not-contact list';
    if (input instanceof HTMLInputElement) input.value = '';
    if (!(history instanceof HTMLElement)) return;
    history.replaceChildren();
    try {
      const result = await fetchJson<{ log?: ContactLog[] }>(`/internal/api/supplier-permits?view=contacts&phone=${encodeURIComponent(contactNumber)}`, { headers: { accept: 'application/json' } });
      for (const entry of result.log ?? []) {
        const li = document.createElement('li');
        const when = new Date(entry.at);
        const stamp = Number.isNaN(when.getTime()) ? entry.at : when.toLocaleString([], { month: 'short', day: 'numeric', hour: 'numeric', minute: '2-digit' });
        li.textContent = [stamp, entry.outcomeLabel, entry.permitId ? `permit ${entry.permitId}` : '', entry.note].filter(Boolean).join(' · ');
        history.append(li);
      }
      if (!history.children.length) {
        const li = document.createElement('li');
        li.textContent = 'No calls logged for this number yet.';
        history.append(li);
      }
    } catch {
      const li = document.createElement('li');
      li.textContent = 'Could not load the history. Close this and try again.';
      history.append(li);
    }
  }

  async function openContact(digits: string, who: string, permitId: string) {
    const dialog = contactDialog();
    if (!(dialog instanceof HTMLDialogElement)) return;
    contactNumber = digits;
    contactWho = who;
    contactPermit = permitId;
    const form = $('[data-contact-form]');
    if (form instanceof HTMLFormElement) form.reset();
    await paintContact();
    if (!dialog.open) dialog.showModal();
  }

  /** After a save the set, the builder table and (when open) the permit list are redrawn so a new block shows everywhere at once. */
  async function refreshContactViews() {
    await loadSupplier();
    if (supplierShown) { supplierShown = false; await loadSupplierRows(); }
  }

  function wireContactDialog() {
    const dialog = contactDialog();
    if (!(dialog instanceof HTMLDialogElement)) return;
    const outcome = $('[data-contact-outcome]');
    if (outcome instanceof HTMLSelectElement && !outcome.options.length) {
      for (const [value, label] of OUTCOMES) outcome.append(new Option(label, value));
    }
    $('[data-contact-close]')?.addEventListener('click', () => dialog.close());
    $('[data-contact-form]')?.addEventListener('submit', async (event) => {
      event.preventDefault();
      const form = event.currentTarget;
      if (!(form instanceof HTMLFormElement)) return;
      const data = new FormData(form);
      const save = $('[data-contact-save]');
      if (save instanceof HTMLButtonElement) save.disabled = true;
      const result = await post({ action: 'log', phone: contactNumber, who: contactWho, permitId: contactPermit, outcome: String(data.get('outcome') || ''), note: String(data.get('note') || '') });
      if (save instanceof HTMLButtonElement) save.disabled = false;
      if (!result.ok) { contactNote(result.error || 'Could not save.'); return; }
      form.reset();
      await refreshContactViews();
      await paintContact();
      contactNote(blockedPhones.has(contactNumber) ? 'Saved. This number is now on the do-not-contact list.' : 'Saved.');
    });
    $('[data-contact-block-form]')?.addEventListener('submit', async (event) => {
      event.preventDefault();
      const form = event.currentTarget;
      if (!(form instanceof HTMLFormElement)) return;
      const why = String(new FormData(form).get('why') || '').trim();
      const lifting = blockedPhones.has(contactNumber);
      if (lifting && !why) { contactNote('Write why this number is coming off the do-not-contact list.'); return; }
      const result = await post(lifting ? { action: 'unblock', phone: contactNumber, note: why } : { action: 'block', phone: contactNumber, reason: 'other', note: why });
      if (!result.ok) { contactNote(result.error || 'Could not save.'); return; }
      await refreshContactViews();
      await paintContact();
      contactNote(lifting ? 'Taken off the do-not-contact list.' : 'Saved. This number is now on the do-not-contact list.');
    });
  }

  function renderPermits(permit: PermitSummary | undefined, failure?: unknown) {
    const message = $('[data-permit-message]');
    const hide = () => { show('[data-permit-stats]', false); show('[data-permit-grid]', false); };
    if (!permit || permit.status !== 'ok' || !permit.homeowners || !permit.newHomes) {
      hide();
      show('[data-permit-message]', true);
      setText('[data-permit-window]', permit?.status === 'empty' ? 'Not loaded' : 'Unavailable');
      if (message instanceof HTMLElement) {
        if (permit?.status === 'empty') message.textContent = 'No permit data has been loaded yet. Build it with npm run build:permit-leads, then load the SQL file into the database. See the Permit leads section of internal/README.md.';
        else message.replaceChildren(loadFailedNode(failure ? loadFailureMessage(failure) : 'Permit data could not be loaded. The rest of this page is unaffected.', isSessionExpired(failure) ? undefined : () => { void loadPermits(); }));
      }
      return;
    }
    const h = permit.homeowners;
    const n = permit.newHomes;
    show('[data-permit-message]', false);
    show('[data-permit-stats]', true);
    show('[data-permit-grid]', true);
    const meta = permit.meta ?? {};
    setText('[data-permit-window]', `${shortDate(meta.window_start ?? '')} to ${shortDate(meta.window_end ?? '')} · loaded ${shortDate((meta.imported_at ?? '').slice(0, 10))}`);
    setText('[data-permit="newHomes"]', count(n.permits));
    setText('[data-permit="newHomesNote"]', `across ${nf.format(n.entities)} lot owners`);
    setText('[data-permit="builders"]', count(n.repeatEntities));
    setText('[data-permit="buildersNote"]', `with 2+ permits · ${nf.format(n.licenseMatched)} matched to a state license`);
    setText('[data-permit="remodels"]', count(h.total));
    setText('[data-permit="remodelsNote"]', `${nf.format(h.absentee)} where the owner lives elsewhere`);
    setText('[data-permit="young"]', count(h.built2011to2016));
    const builders = permit.builders ?? [];
    setChart('permitMonthly', {
      build: (width) => (n.byMonth.length ? columnChart(n.byMonth.map((r) => ({ label: monthLabel(r.label), value: r.value })), { width, title: 'New-home permits issued per month' }) : ''),
      empty: 'No new-home permits in this window.',
    });
    setChart('permitBuilders', {
      build: (width) => barChart(builders.slice(0, 8).map((b) => ({ label: b.name, value: b.permits })), { width, title: 'Builders by new-home permits' }),
      empty: 'No builders in this window.',
    });
    setChart('permitSignals', {
      build: (width) => barChart(h.signals.map((s) => ({ label: s.label, value: s.value })), { width, title: 'Remodel permits by fit signal' }),
      empty: 'No remodel permits in this window.',
    });
    setChart('permitDecades', {
      build: (width) => (h.decades.length ? columnChart(h.decades, { width, title: 'Remodel permits by decade the home was built' }) : ''),
      empty: 'No year-built data.',
    });
    const body = $('[data-builder-rows]');
    if (!(body instanceof HTMLElement)) return;
    body.replaceChildren();
    if (!builders.length) {
      const tr = document.createElement('tr');
      const td = document.createElement('td');
      td.colSpan = 7;
      td.className = 'an-empty';
      td.textContent = 'No builders in this window.';
      tr.append(td);
      body.append(tr);
      return;
    }
    for (const b of builders) {
      const license = b.license;
      const licenseText = license
        ? `${license.business} · ${license.number}${license.status && license.status !== 'ACTIVE' ? ` · ${license.status}` : ''}${/verify/.test(license.match) ? ' · name match, verify' : ''}`
        : 'None found by exact name';
      appendRow(body, [b.name, nf.format(b.permits), nf.format(b.issued30d), nf.format(b.issued90d), b.subdivisions.join(', ') || '—', licenseText, license ? phoneCell(license.phone) : '—']);
    }
  }

  async function loadPermits() {
    try {
      renderPermits(await fetchJson<PermitSummary>('/internal/api/permit-leads', { headers: { accept: 'application/json' } }));
    } catch (error) {
      renderPermits(undefined, error);
    }
  }

  let homeownersShown = false;
  async function loadHomeowners() {
    const button = $('[data-homeowners-load]');
    const body = $('[data-homeowner-rows]');
    if (!(button instanceof HTMLButtonElement) || !(body instanceof HTMLElement)) return;
    if (homeownersShown) {
      homeownersShown = false;
      show('[data-homeowners-wrap]', false);
      button.textContent = 'Show the list';
      return;
    }
    button.disabled = true;
    try {
      const rows = (await fetchJson<{ rows?: HomeownerLead[] }>('/internal/api/permit-leads?view=homeowners&limit=150', { headers: { accept: 'application/json' } })).rows ?? [];
      body.replaceChildren();
      for (const r of rows) {
        const mail = r.ownerMailing ? (r.absentee ? `Elsewhere: ${r.ownerMailing}` : 'At the property') : '—';
        const sold = r.lastSaleDate ? `${shortDate(r.lastSaleDate)}${typeof r.lastSaleCents === 'number' ? ` · ${dollars(r.lastSaleCents)}` : ''}` : '—';
        appendRow(body, [r.address || '(no address)', shortDate(r.permitDate), r.workType || '—', r.yearBuilt ? String(r.yearBuilt) : '—', `${r.owner || '—'}${r.ownerApplied ? ' (applied)' : ''}`, mail, sold, `${r.score} of 5`]);
      }
      if (!rows.length) {
        const tr = document.createElement('tr');
        const td = document.createElement('td');
        td.colSpan = 8;
        td.className = 'an-empty';
        td.textContent = 'No remodel permits loaded.';
        tr.append(td);
        body.append(tr);
      }
      homeownersShown = true;
      show('[data-homeowners-wrap]', true);
      button.textContent = 'Hide the list';
    } catch (error) {
      setText('[data-status]', loadFailureMessage(error, 'Could not load the permit list. Try again.'));
    } finally {
      button.disabled = false;
    }
  }

  // ---------- supplier permit list ----------
  // Only the remodel-style groups get the fit score; the endpoint sends a score for every row, so the page decides what to show.
  const SCORED_GROUPS = ['remodel', 'adu', 'reroof'];
  const editionLabel = (value: string) => {
    const m = /^(\d{4})-W(\d{2})$/.exec(value);
    return m ? `Week ${Number(m[2])}, ${m[1]}` : value || 'Latest report';
  };

  function emptyRow(body: HTMLElement, columns: number, text: string) {
    const tr = document.createElement('tr');
    const td = document.createElement('td');
    td.colSpan = columns;
    td.className = 'an-empty';
    td.textContent = text;
    tr.append(td);
    body.append(tr);
  }

  function fillGroupSelect(groups: { key: string; label: string; value: number }[]) {
    const select = $('[data-supplier-group]');
    if (!(select instanceof HTMLSelectElement)) return;
    const keep = select.value;
    select.replaceChildren();
    const all = document.createElement('option');
    all.value = '';
    all.textContent = 'Everything';
    select.append(all);
    for (const g of groups) {
      const option = document.createElement('option');
      option.value = g.key;
      option.textContent = `${g.label} (${nf.format(g.value)})`;
      select.append(option);
    }
    select.value = groups.some((g) => g.key === keep) ? keep : '';
    updateSupplierCsv();
  }

  function updateSupplierCsv() {
    const select = $('[data-supplier-group]');
    const link = $('[data-supplier-csv]');
    if (!(select instanceof HTMLSelectElement) || !(link instanceof HTMLAnchorElement)) return;
    link.href = `/internal/api/supplier-permits?view=csv${select.value ? `&group=${encodeURIComponent(select.value)}` : ''}`;
  }

  /** The same project in our other records, one line each: what it is, its number (a link when the Command Center has a page), the name, and how it matched. */
  function connectionCell(connections: SupplierConnection[]): string | HTMLElement {
    if (!connections.length) return 'New to us';
    const list = document.createElement('div');
    list.className = 'an-conn-list';
    for (const c of connections) {
      const item = document.createElement('div');
      item.className = 'an-conn';
      const label = document.createElement('strong');
      label.textContent = c.label;
      item.append(label);
      if (c.number) {
        item.append(' ');
        if (c.href.startsWith('/internal/')) {
          const link = document.createElement('a');
          link.href = c.href;
          link.textContent = c.number;
          item.append(link);
        } else {
          const number = document.createElement('span');
          number.className = 'an-conn-no';
          number.textContent = c.number;
          item.append(number);
        }
      }
      if (c.name) item.append(` · ${c.name}`);
      const note = [c.detail, c.how].filter(Boolean).join(' · ');
      if (note) {
        const small = document.createElement('small');
        small.textContent = note;
        item.append(small);
      }
      list.append(item);
    }
    return list;
  }

  /** A builder's permits from this report, opened under its row: permit number, address, subdivision, date, value and what each connects to. */
  function builderPermitsTable(rows: SupplierRow[]): HTMLElement {
    const table = document.createElement('table');
    table.className = 'an-table an-table-list an-mini-table';
    const head = document.createElement('thead');
    const headRow = document.createElement('tr');
    for (const title of ['Permit', 'Address', 'Subdivision', 'Date', 'Value', 'Connected to']) {
      const th = document.createElement('th');
      th.scope = 'col';
      th.textContent = title;
      headRow.append(th);
    }
    head.append(headRow);
    const body = document.createElement('tbody');
    for (const r of rows) {
      appendRow(body, [`${r.id}${r.pending ? ' (pending)' : ''}`, `${r.address || '(no address)'}${r.city ? `, ${r.city}` : ''}`, r.subdivision || '—', shortDate(r.permitDate), r.valueCents ? dollars(r.valueCents) : '—', connectionCell(r.connections ?? [])]);
    }
    table.append(head, body);
    return table;
  }

  function builderProjectsButton(b: SupplierBuilder): HTMLElement {
    const idle = `Show ${nf.format(b.permits)} permit${b.permits === 1 ? '' : 's'}`;
    const button = document.createElement('button');
    button.type = 'button';
    button.className = 'btn btn-ghost an-mini';
    button.textContent = idle;
    button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
    button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      const row = button.closest('tr');
      if (!row || !b.key) return;
      const open = row.nextElementSibling;
      if (open instanceof HTMLElement && open.dataset.builderDetail === b.key) {
        open.remove();
        button.textContent = idle;
        button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'false');
        return;
      }
      button.disabled = true;
      try {
        const result = await fetchJson<{ rows?: SupplierRow[]; total?: number }>(`/internal/api/supplier-permits?view=list&limit=100&builder=${encodeURIComponent(b.key)}`, { headers: { accept: 'application/json' } });
        const rows = result.rows ?? [];
        const detail = document.createElement('tr');
        detail.dataset.builderDetail = b.key;
        const cell = document.createElement('td');
        cell.colSpan = 9;
        cell.className = 'an-detail';
        if (rows.length) cell.append(builderPermitsTable(rows));
        else cell.textContent = 'No permits found for this builder.';
        if ((result.total ?? rows.length) > rows.length) {
          const more = document.createElement('p');
          more.className = 'an-note';
          more.textContent = `Showing ${nf.format(rows.length)} of ${nf.format(result.total ?? rows.length)}. The spreadsheet has all of them.`;
          cell.append(more);
        }
        detail.append(cell);
        row.after(detail);
        button.textContent = 'Hide permits';
        button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', 'true');
      } catch (error) {
        setText('[data-status]', loadFailureMessage(error, 'Could not load that builder\'s permits. Try again.'));
      } finally {
        button.disabled = false;
      }
    });
    return button;
  }

  function renderSupplier(data: SupplierSummary | undefined, failure?: unknown) {
    const message = $('[data-supplier-message]');
    if (!data || data.status !== 'ok' || !data.totals || !data.meta) {
      show('[data-supplier-stats]', false);
      show('[data-supplier-grid]', false);
      show('[data-supplier-message]', true);
      setText('[data-supplier-window]', data?.status === 'empty' ? 'Not loaded' : 'Unavailable');
      if (message instanceof HTMLElement) {
        if (data?.status === 'empty') message.textContent = 'No supplier list loaded yet. Build it with npm run build:supplier-permits from the weekly report, then load the SQL file into the database. See the Supplier permit list section of internal/README.md.';
        else message.replaceChildren(loadFailedNode(failure ? loadFailureMessage(failure) : 'The supplier list could not be loaded. The rest of this page is unaffected.', isSessionExpired(failure) ? undefined : () => { void loadSupplier(); }));
      }
      return;
    }
    const t = data.totals;
    const meta = data.meta;
    show('[data-supplier-message]', false);
    show('[data-supplier-stats]', true);
    show('[data-supplier-grid]', true);
    const editions = data.editions?.length ?? 0;
    setText('[data-supplier-window]', `${editionLabel(meta.edition)} · ${shortDate(meta.edition_start)} to ${shortDate(meta.edition_end)} · loaded ${shortDate(meta.imported_at.slice(0, 10))}${editions > 1 ? ` · ${editions} weeks in total` : ''}`);
    setText('[data-supplier="permits"]', count(t.permits));
    setText('[data-supplier="permitsNote"]', t.pending ? `${nf.format(t.pending)} still pending approval` : 'all approved');
    setText('[data-supplier="fresh"]', count(t.newToLists));
    setText('[data-supplier="freshNote"]', `${nf.format(t.inPermitLeads)} already in permit leads · ${nf.format(t.inMailPilot)} in the mail pilot${t.inClearviewWork ? ` · ${nf.format(t.inClearviewWork)} on a street with a Clearview quote or job` : ''}${meta.xref_asof ? ` (compared ${shortDate(meta.xref_asof.slice(0, 10))})` : ''}`);
    setText('[data-supplier="phones"]', count(t.withOwnerPhone));
    setText('[data-supplier="parcels"]', count(t.parcelMatched));
    setText('[data-supplier="parcelsNote"]', `of ${nf.format(t.permits)} · the rest have no street or no single match`);
    const groups = data.groups ?? [];
    fillGroupSelect(groups);
    setChart('supplierGroups', {
      build: (width) => barChart(groups.map((g) => ({ label: g.label, value: g.value })), { width, title: 'Supplier permits by type' }),
      empty: 'No permits loaded.',
    });
    const signals = data.scored?.signals ?? [];
    setChart('supplierSignals', {
      build: (width) => ((data.scored?.total ?? 0) > 0 ? barChart(signals.map((s) => ({ label: s.label, value: s.value })), { width, title: `${data.scored?.total ?? 0} remodel, ADU and re-roof permits by fit signal` }) : ''),
      empty: 'No remodel, ADU or re-roof permits in this report.',
    });
    const body = $('[data-supplier-builder-rows]');
    if (!(body instanceof HTMLElement)) return;
    body.replaceChildren();
    const builders = data.builders ?? [];
    if (!builders.length) {
      emptyRow(body, 9, 'No new-home builders in this report.');
      return;
    }
    for (const b of builders) {
      const tracked = b.tracked ? `Yes: ${b.tracked}` : b.related ? `Check: ${b.related}` : '—';
      const license = b.license ? `${b.license.number}${b.license.status && b.license.status !== 'ACTIVE' ? ` · ${b.license.status}` : ''}` : 'None found by exact name';
      const metro = b.metro ? `#${b.metro.rank} · ${nf.format(b.metro.homes)} homes this year` : '—';
      appendRow(body, [b.name, nf.format(b.permits), b.valueCents ? dollars(b.valueCents) : '—', shortDate(b.lastDate), metro, tracked, license, phoneCell(b.phone), builderProjectsButton(b)]);
    }
  }

  async function loadSupplier() {
    await loadContacts();
    try {
      renderSupplier(await fetchJson<SupplierSummary>('/internal/api/supplier-permits', { headers: { accept: 'application/json' } }));
    } catch (error) {
      renderSupplier(undefined, error);
    }
  }

  let supplierShown = false;
  async function loadSupplierRows() {
    const button = $('[data-supplier-load]');
    const select = $('[data-supplier-group]');
    const body = $('[data-supplier-rows]');
    if (!(button instanceof HTMLButtonElement) || !(select instanceof HTMLSelectElement) || !(body instanceof HTMLElement)) return;
    if (supplierShown) {
      supplierShown = false;
      show('[data-supplier-wrap]', false);
      show('[data-supplier-count]', false);
      button.textContent = 'Show the list';
      return;
    }
    button.disabled = true;
    try {
      const group = select.value;
      const result = await fetchJson<{ rows?: SupplierRow[]; total?: number }>(`/internal/api/supplier-permits?view=list&limit=300${group ? `&group=${encodeURIComponent(group)}` : ''}`, { headers: { accept: 'application/json' } });
      const rows = result.rows ?? [];
      body.replaceChildren();
      for (const r of rows) {
        const scored = SCORED_GROUPS.includes(r.group);
        const mail = r.ownerMailing ? (r.absentee ? `Elsewhere: ${r.ownerMailing}` : 'At the property') : '—';
        const licensed = Boolean(r.stateLicense || r.builderLicense);
        const contractor = r.builder ? `${r.builder}${r.stateLicense ? ` · ${r.stateLicense.number}` : r.builderLicense ? ` · ${r.builderLicense}` : ''}` : '—';
        const home = [r.yearBuilt ? String(r.yearBuilt) : '', r.sqft ? `${nf.format(r.sqft)} sq ft` : ''].filter(Boolean).join(' · ') || '—';
        const sold = r.lastSaleDate ? `${shortDate(r.lastSaleDate)}${typeof r.lastSaleCents === 'number' ? ` · ${dollars(r.lastSaleCents)}` : ''}` : '—';
        const work = `${r.permitType || r.groupLabel}${typeof r.valueCents === 'number' ? ` · ${dollars(r.valueCents)}` : ''}`;
        const address = document.createElement('span');
        address.append(`${r.address || '(no address)'}${r.city ? `, ${r.city}` : ''}`);
        if (r.subdivision) {
          const sub = document.createElement('small');
          sub.className = 'an-sub';
          sub.textContent = r.subdivision;
          address.append(sub);
        }
        // An owner's phone is shown as text on purpose (see the note above); only a licensed contractor's number is a link.
        const contractorCell = document.createElement('span');
        contractorCell.append(contractor);
        if (r.builderPhone) contractorCell.append(' · ', phoneCell(r.builderPhone, { who: 'builder', permitId: r.id, link: licensed }));
        appendRow(body, [address, `${shortDate(r.permitDate)} · ${r.id}${r.pending ? ' (pending)' : ''}`, work, connectionCell(r.connections ?? []), r.owner || '—', mail, r.ownerPhone ? phoneCell(r.ownerPhone, { who: 'owner', permitId: r.id, link: false }) : '—', contractorCell, home, sold, scored ? `${r.score} of 5` : '—']);
      }
      if (!rows.length) emptyRow(body, 11, 'No permits in this group.');
      const total = result.total ?? rows.length;
      setText('[data-supplier-count]', total > rows.length ? `Showing the best ${nf.format(rows.length)} of ${nf.format(total)}. The spreadsheet has all of them.` : `${nf.format(rows.length)} permit${rows.length === 1 ? '' : 's'}.`);
      show('[data-supplier-count]', true);
      supplierShown = true;
      show('[data-supplier-wrap]', true);
      button.textContent = 'Hide the list';
    } catch (error) {
      setText('[data-status]', loadFailureMessage(error, 'Could not load the supplier list. Try again.'));
    } finally {
      button.disabled = false;
    }
  }

  async function load() {
    const button = $('[data-refresh]');
    if (button instanceof HTMLButtonElement) button.disabled = true;
    setText('[data-status]', 'Loading permits…');
    try {
      await Promise.all([loadPermits(), loadSupplier()]);
      setText('[data-status]', `Checked ${new Date().toLocaleTimeString()}. See each list for its status.`);
    } finally {
      if (button instanceof HTMLButtonElement) button.disabled = false;
    }
  }
  document.querySelector('[data-homeowners-load]')?.addEventListener('click', loadHomeowners);
  document.querySelector('[data-supplier-load]')?.addEventListener('click', loadSupplierRows);
  document.querySelector('[data-supplier-group]')?.addEventListener('change', () => {
    updateSupplierCsv();
    if (supplierShown) { supplierShown = false; void loadSupplierRows(); }
  });
  document.querySelector('[data-refresh]')?.addEventListener('click', load);
  wireContactDialog();
  load();
</script>
<style>
  .an-hero{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:end;gap:var(--space-m);margin-bottom:var(--space-m)}
  .an-hero h1{margin:.08rem 0 .35rem}
  .an-section{margin-bottom:var(--space-l)}
  .an-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:end;gap:var(--space-s);margin-bottom:.4rem}
  .an-head h2{margin:.1rem 0 0}
  .an-meta{font-size:var(--step--2);font-weight:750;color:var(--ink-soft)}
  .an-note{margin:0 0 var(--space-s);color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:var(--step--1)}
  .an-callout{margin:0 0 var(--space-s);padding:.85rem 1rem;border:1px solid var(--line);border-left:3px solid var(--accent);border-radius:var(--radius);background:var(--paper-sunk);font-size:var(--step--1)}
  .an-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:var(--space-s)}
  .an-wide{grid-column:1/-1}
  .an-panel{min-width:0;padding:1rem 1.05rem;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-lg);background:var(--paper-raised);box-shadow:var(--shadow-sm)}
  .an-panel h3{margin:0 0 .5rem;font-size:var(--step-0)}
  /* Rows are built by script after load, so Astro's scoped-style attribute is absent; these must be global. */
  :global(.an-row){position:relative;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:.75rem;padding:.55rem 0 .7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
  :global(.an-row:last-child){border-bottom:0}
  :global(.an-row-label){min-width:0;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font-size:var(--step--1)}
  :global(.an-row strong){font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
  :global(.an-row i){position:absolute;left:0;bottom:.3rem;height:3px;border-radius:2px;background:var(--accent);opacity:.55}
  :global(.an-empty){margin:0;color:var(--ink-soft);font-size:var(--step--1)}
  /* Charts are built by script (see src/lib/charts.ts), so these must be global. */
  :global(.an-chart){min-width:0}
  :global(svg.ch){--ch-1:var(--accent);--ch-2:#3a3d42;--ch-3:#b7791f;--ch-4:#2b6cb0;--ch-5:#b83280;--ch-6:#8a8d93;display:block;width:100%;height:auto;overflow:visible;font-family:inherit}
  :global(.ch-label){font-size:12px;fill:var(--ink)}
  :global(.ch-axis){font-size:11px;fill:var(--ink-soft)}
  :global(.ch-value){font-size:12px;font-weight:650;fill:var(--ink);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
  :global(.ch-center){font-size:20px;font-weight:700;fill:var(--ink);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
  :global(.ch-barvalue){font-size:12px;font-weight:700;fill:var(--ink);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;paint-order:stroke;stroke:var(--paper-raised);stroke-width:3px;stroke-linejoin:round}
  :global(.ch-grid){stroke:var(--line);stroke-width:1}
  :global(.ch-track){fill:var(--paper-sunk)}
  :global(.ch-zero){fill:var(--line-strong)}
